WEBVTT

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.150
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.630
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:10.390
Today, we meet a brother and sister acrobatic team!

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:14.030
Everyone is shooting to win the New Year's talent competition.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.980
It's time for the first greeting of the new year!

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.910
Happy New Year!

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.460
Here's to another great year!

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.020
Doki!

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.410
Pyon Pyon

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.570
Fumu Fumu

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.480
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.080
Howa Howa

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.280
Kira Kira

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.210
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.970
What color is your egg?

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.750
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.790
Even if you say mean things,

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.640
I know you really love me.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.310
Even if we fight a lot,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.980
it's just 'cause we're always together.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.040
Because you believe in me,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.800
I can do anything!

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:14.100
And that's why I unlock my heart!

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.810
The person you want to be; things you want to say.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.470
Important things; things that are true.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.180
Who you are; what you've yet to realize.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.830
Mysterious things; happy things.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:35.740
All of these things are inside your egg!

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.880
Pyon Pyon

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.030
Fumu Fumu

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:41.970
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.520
Howa Howa

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.730
Kira Kira

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.680
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.420
What color is your egg?

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.230
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:26.220
Bravo, Maman! She is truly dazzling on the stage!

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:31.200
Her reindeer dance the other day was good, and she can even do magic?

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.910
Your mama-san can do just 'bout anything!

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:38.570
But Maman is at her best when she's acting, I'm sure of it.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.180
Did you say something?

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.640
Nothing.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:48.660
New Year's! Character Transformation Comedy Special!

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:48.660
Episode 64

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.440
There are so many people!

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.180
Hurry up, Amu-chan!

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.040
Jeez, wait for me.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.800
Hinamori-san!

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.250
Over here.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:11.350
And now that we're all here...

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:14.350
Happy New Year!

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.310
Happy New Year!

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.600
Let's do our best this year, Hinamori-san.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.850
Yes, let's.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:29.170
Is it weird for me to be in a kimono?

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.120
It looks great on you!

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.770
Thank you.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.520
I guess all the time it took to put on was worth it.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.080
It sure was.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.090
Don't you think, Amu-chan?

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:40.970
Oh, be quiet!

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:45.510
Tadase didn't compliment <i>our</i> kimonos, though.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:48.060
Yaya, this can only mean...

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.490
You two look wonderful!

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.520
Let's go pray, okay? {literally, "let's go" where "go" is the humble form used only in keigo or to refer to when you "go" pray at the alter}

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.370
There sure are all kinds of shops.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.730
It is so hard to choose!

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.930
What is it, Amu-chi?

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.580
An astrological fortune-telling lottery?

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.060
Sounds like a blast!

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.100
"Average luck."

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.950
"The stars might shine most brightly on your school or workplace."

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:29.890
All right!

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:31.670
Rima got "small luck!"

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.460
Right in the middle.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.080
It'd be way more interesting to get "great luck" or "great misfortune."

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:39.950
I also got "small luck."

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:41.250
What about you, Hotori-kun?

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.190
"Great misfortune."

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:45.240
"Watch out for black holes."

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.020
I guess that rules out world domination for this year-dechu.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.590
What about you, Amu-chi?

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:51.590
"Great luck!"

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:52.910
{hontou?}Really?

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:57.000
"You'll have an encounter like a shooting star falling upon you."

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.060
An encounter like a shooting star?

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.910
How romantic!

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:02.910
A prediction about your love life, huh?

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.970
Yeah right, as if.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.920
Perhaps it means you'll make a new friend.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.620
A new friend?

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.960
All right, bring it!

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.310
Get ready!

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.600
Here!

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:20.600
That's the way!

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.930
Here's the second one!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.430
And one more!

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:39.250
We screwed up again.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.130
Wow!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:48.770
I'm Ebihara You, and this is my sister.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:49.890
Ebihara Kiko.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:54.450
We're going to be participating in this shrine's talent competition.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.950
Talent competition?

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:59.400
Yeah! They hold one at this shrine every year.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:05.060
It's a competition where amateurs perform for an audience.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:11.060
I was thinking we'd try out this time around, so we've been practicing over the last year.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.650
Oh? That's amazing.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:16.180
But we still can't do it right.

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:19.640
Well, we have no trouble with one ball.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.290
Fine.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:26.530
Be it the performing arts or comedy, the desire to entertain an audience is one and the same.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.430
Rima?

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.960
I will assist you.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.350
Me, too!

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.110
Sounds fun! Count me in!

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:37.550
Then we will as well.

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:38.560
Sure.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.110
Cool! Do you think I could do it?

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.460
Sure thing! With a little practice.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.930
I wonder if I should invite Lulu?

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:55.560
As I've written in my reports so far, the Embryo has already shown itself to me.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.430
I believe it is only a matter of time before I secure it.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.180
You really think you can do it-nya?

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:05.670
It's ny-ot like y'all found it, neither!

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.560
Stop talking like me-nya!

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.510
It's not nya, it's y'all! {here we go again...}

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.720
To be frank, I wonder if I've expected too much of you.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:16.230
What do you mean?

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:21.340
You're taking too much time. You should be partnering with Ikuto.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:26.640
I'm working very hard! If you have complaints, tell them to Ikuto!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.220
If I may be excused!

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:37.060
She's a real troublemaker.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:44.200
Speaking of which, we had an intruder the other day.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:48.810
He was filmed on the security cameras, but we can't tell who it was.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:53.310
I think he understands now what happens when someone goes against Easter.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:57.260
That goes for you, too. Do not even think of rebelling.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.280
Not for a single moment.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:02.560
I am your father, after all.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.470
Do not even consider it.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:11.040
Those born into the Tsukiyomi house cannot turn against Easter.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.530
Never forget that.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.720
I know.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.220
I'm going home.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.390
He was unusually obedient today.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:27.770
Maybe that beating he got knocked some sense into him.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:30.260
Ikuto, it worked perfectly-nya.

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.600
The key to the violin-nya!

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:39.190
While that guy was yelling at you so smugly, I grabbed it-nya!

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:43.370
Let's go!

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.490
Yeah!

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:48.810
We're finished with injecting the X Eggs' energy.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:51.980
All that's left are the final adjustments.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.460
What's the matter, Chief?

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:00.490
I spilled the beans about the violin's key to Tsukiyomi Ikuto!

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:02.720
What'll I do if the Director finds out?!

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.060
Bit late for that.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:06.960
Tsukiyomi Ikuto!

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.560
Th-That key!

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:15.740
If you want to keep the fact that you blabbed about the key quiet, you'll do as you're told.

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:24.300
You're the one who tied us up, okay?!

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:27.290
You came out of nowhere and attacked us, all right?!

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:31.430
There it is-nya!

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:37.750
There's an unidentified intruder in the research labs!

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:38.840
Hurry-nya!

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:47.750
Over there, over there!

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.430
The violin was stolen.

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:56.890
Damn it! Find the intruder!

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.600
You're not going to get us like last time-nya.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:13.310
You've got to be kidding me. What does he mean, work together?

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:16.400
No kidding! Do they take you for a fool, Lulu?

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.060
Lulu! What a coincidence!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.400
Could this be...

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:31.070
The encounter like a shooting star?

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:35.520
Like a shooting star, Lulu-chan and Nana-chan appear!

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.780
Let me introduce you to everyone.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:52.190
Lulu De Morcerf Yamamoto-san!

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:53.930
You can leave off the Yamamoto, thank you.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.520
Nice to meet you.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:56.590
Same here.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.690
Hey, hey! Aren't you a Character Bearer, too, Lulu-chi?

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:00.930
Lulu-chi?

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.040
This is Lulu-chan's Guardian Character.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.810
Nana-chan!

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:05.940
I'm Nana, y'all!

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:06.870
Y'all?

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.180
What's up with that-dechu? {you should talk!}

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.890
You're that girl everyone's talking about, right?

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:14.000
The one whose mom is the actress Mayuzumi Kahoru-san.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:18.590
She won an award at the international film festival, right?

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:21.990
Angel in the Mist was an incredible movie.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.130
Naturally.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.140
It's my mother's greatest work.

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:29.260
She's been appearing on a lot of variety shows lately, hasn't she?

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:33.510
Did I say something wrong?

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.560
How long do you guys plan on slacking off?

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:39.310
And you, over there!

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:41.120
Don't get in our way!

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:41.860
Huh?

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:44.170
Let's practice together!

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:49.950
So what exactly are you guys doing?

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.320
Well, you see...

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.430
The environment!

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:55.600
It's crucial for a performer to adapt to their surrounding environment!

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:58.640
Everyone spin their umbrellas and create their own feel for it!

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.470
It's something like that.

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:03.920
Don't forget the smile!

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:08.460
No matter how frustrating it is, you mustn't show the audience anything except how easy it is for you!

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:09.350
Right!

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:27.270
Awesome!

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:28.470
Lulu, that's incredible!

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:31.010
Have you been formally trained?

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.010
I don't need training for something simple like this.

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.170
We have to do our best as well!

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:38.970
Yeah!

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.070
Brother, smile!

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.490
You're amazing, Lulu.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:50.040
You can make jewelry and do the umbrella spinning trick.

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.760
You can do anything.

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:53.930
Oh, it's nothing really.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:57.530
Hey, what's your favorite thing to do, Lulu?

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:02.640
W-Well...

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.310
Where are you going?

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:12.980
It's none of your business.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:17.560
I wonder what happened.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.000
Search for Ikuto, they say?

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:25.340
That's right! At this rate, we won't be able to finish the plan with his violin!

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:27.200
It's the Director's order!

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:32.510
What's with them? Didn't I say I'd capture the Embryo?!

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:34.220
Well, that's...

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:38.760
Y'all got somethin' else up your sleeves in case Lulu fails?

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:42.010
Well, to hell with y'all!

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:46.240
You've definitely got the feel for it.

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.400
Do not forget it.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:49.630
Thank you.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:52.680
We'll practice a bit more.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:54.160
See you later, then!

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.130
All right, we'll see you at the grounds.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.600
I wonder what was up with Lulu.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:04.470
Jeez, they're treatin' me like a fool!

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:06.010
Damn straight!

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.150
What is it, Nana?

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:11.330
I can sense the presence of a Guardian Character.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:26.030
We should be fine now that we've gotten this far-nya.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:28.930
Something wrong with you, Ikuto?

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:34.640
Ikuto, there's something weird about this violin.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:39.720
You...

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:42.010
We're not handing over the violin-nya!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:45.140
You don't plan on giving it back to Easter?

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:50.390
What do you intend to do with it?

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:55.180
Use it to call out the Embryo and grant your own wish?

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.270
It's none of your business.

00:14:58.270 --> 00:14:59.260
Yes, it is.

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.000
I'll be the one to obtain the Embryo.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:06.260
I won't hand it over to you, or to Easter!

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:10.680
I guess you're not just a puppet, after all.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:15.460
And I suppose you're no mere house cat.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:21.120
Hey, didn't you come to catch Ikuto?

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:25.380
I don't pick on the weak.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:28.100
Victories like that don't please me.

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:31.790
There's a bunch of Easter's goons around here.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.330
Hurry up and get somewhere safe, y'hear?

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:37.920
Thank you-nya.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:42.420
Ikuto, what is it? Are you okay?

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.010
We just can't do it right, can we?

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:58.050
What'll we do if we screw up during the actual performance?

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:02.200
Maybe we should just give it up for this year.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.560
You're lost, aren't you?

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:08.470
You're...

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:25.530
Doesn't look like Kiko and You are here yet.

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:27.640
It's about to start!

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:29.630
That feeling!

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.980
I feel it, too-dechu!

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:31.810
Yeah!

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:38.930
Let's put on a show, Brother.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:44.850
Yeah. Let's show our act to the entire world!

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:58.990
Character Transformation: Happy Dream #1!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:01.010
And #2!

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:04.180
Watch our act!

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:10.930
Tadase-kun.

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:13.430
Let's go, guys!

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:17.120
My heart:

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.550
My heart:

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:19.770
My heart:

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.280
My heart:

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:22.740
Unlock!

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:51.640
Character Transformation: Platinum Royal!

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:56.310
Character Transformation: Clown Drop!

00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:59.760
Character Transformation: Dear Baby!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:03.880
Character Transformation: Amulet Heart!

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:17.760
They're really into it!

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:20.720
Get a move on! Get to it! {this seems to be Nana's catch phrase.... it's the third time she's said it or something very similar}

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:24.140
Come on out, Embryo!

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:27.760
We won't screw up anymore, Brother!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:30.890
Stop it, you two! Listen to me!

00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:34.180
Watch our perfect performance!

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:38.450
Everyone!

